config.py
signals.db
signals.db-shm
signals.db-wal
content_cache.json
# `cache/*`, NOT `cache/` — a file cannot be re-included if its PARENT
# DIRECTORY is excluded, so `cache/` followed by `!cache/nifty500.csv` silently
# does nothing. Same gitignore semantics the .vercelignore header documents.
cache/*
# The Nifty 500 constituent list is an INPUT, not a cache: stock_screen reads it
# and refuses to run without it. It was ignored along with everything else in
# cache/, so the workflow checked out a tree with no universe file and died on
# its first line with "universe unavailable". 33KB, changes when NSE rebalances.
!cache/nifty500.csv
# Same reasoning for the Total Market list, and the stakes are higher: NSE
# routinely 403s datacenter IPs, so a CI run that cannot fetch it falls back
# to the 500 list and silently screens 500 names instead of 750 with nothing
# in the log to say the universe shrank. Committing it makes the fetch an
# optimisation rather than a dependency.
!cache/nifty_total_market.csv
logs/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
.vercel
node_modules/
package-lock.json
test-results/
